    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Following the successful completion of the first phase in August 2023 and training of 20 healthcare workers, 10 from each districts of Dadu and Sanghar as the master trainers, the Aga Khan University's Centre of Excellence for Trauma and Emergencies (AKU-CETE) has shifted focus to the rollout phase of its Integrated Disaster Response Programme. The initial phase saw the training of healthcare workers from Dadu and Sanghar as master trainers, laying the foundation for the ongoing dissemination of crucial knowledge and skills.",
